# Manuscript PDF page 84

                       HERALDS OF THE CEMÍ



   It took a while to find. Two years of texts, two years of nothing.
There it was, near the bottom of a conversation I’d never muted and
never opened: you up. Two words, gray bubble, 1:14 a.m. Under it, Read.
Under that, white space, two years of it.
   I typed, yeah. i’m up.
   I looked at it until the screen dimmed.
   Then I hit send, and the little word underneath it said Delivered,
which meant the number still worked, which meant a phone some‐
where in the Bronx had just lit up in somebody’s pocket.
   Three dots appeared.
   I watched them. I didn’t breathe. They pulsed there, rising and fall‐
ing, a person typing and deleting and typing, and I counted without
wanting to, one, two, three.
   They lasted eight seconds. Then they stopped.




